{
	title: 'Questions: durable forms in the session',
	spec: 'The one way Hal asks a human something, as specified in tasks/w4/forms.md (sections Forms and In a block). A question is a form (text with placeholder, secret, choice including y/N and single press-Enter) written to history, shown as a block, answerable from any client (first answer wins), surviving restart; while one is open the session is blocked (question) per tasks/j1/states.md. Secrets travel over the connection as-is and history records only that one was provided. Terminal and web both render and answer them, sharing form state and key handling from common code. Prove it with a synthetic model that asks "How should I call you?" and uses the answer. The Model picker section of forms.md is the shared reference for task zg and reflects its current deliberately promoted GPT Sol family default.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Shape: src/common/forms.ts holds Form/Field (text, secret, choice; y/N is choice ['yes','no'] initial 1, press-Enter is a one-option choice), check/redact of answers, forms.open(records) (the unanswered question in the unfinished turn), and the shared key handling forms.step(FormState, Key) -> { state, action: submit | cancel }. forms.follow keeps a client's typed values while the same question stays open. Checkboxes, level and tree fields are not built yet: add them as Field types with step() cases and a table test.",
		'History: `question` { id, form } and `answer` { question, answers, secrets? } records. Secret values never reach history or events: the answer record lists them in `secrets`; only the `answer` command carries them, and the host hands them to whoever asked in memory at once. replay.toMessages skips both records: real models never see them.',
		"Host: host.ask(id, form) parks the running turn (history.park: no turn end; since 6f the usage of its rounds so far is kept in the question record and carried on), appends the question, broadcasts `question`, and moves the state to blocked { reason: 'question' }. states.fromHistory derives the same from an open question, so recover() leaves it alone after a restart. host.reply (the `answer` command) refuses anything but the open question (first answer wins), checks answers against the form, records, broadcasts `answer`, then host.start(id, undefined, answers) re-runs the turn. Escape pauses as usual; the paused turn end closes the question and continue re-runs (it asks again).",
		'Synthetic models: src/host/synthetic.ts, model ids hal/<name>, (records, answers?) => { say?, ask? }, run by runTurn in place of a provider round. hal/intro is the proof. Only synthetic models (and later commands) ask; real models get no ask tool.',
		"For et (commands): add an asker to the question record (say `from: { command, args }`) and make host.reply re-run that command's run(args, answers) instead of host.start when the question came from a command; a command question is outside any turn, so decide how its blocked state ends (probably: state from forms.open alone, with no turn). For 6f (approval): ask from inside runTurn before tools.run, one y/N form per matching call; on reply re-run the turn and have it find the answered question for the pending calls (history already holds the calls without results; replay treats them as missing, so 6f must run them itself before the next provider round). The highlighted part of the call needs a field or form text markup both clients can render; forms have none yet.",
		'For kv (modals): forms.step and FormState are client-neutral, so a modal can reuse them unchanged; frame.formLines(form, width) renders one as rows with a cursor, which a modal can place in its box. Web: page.formNode/syncForm render a form as DOM with native inputs (text typing is native; view.key maps browser keys, and enter/escape/tab/up/down go through forms.step).',
		'Clients: while a question is open, terminal keys go to the form (app.state.form), the prompt keeps its text; the web disables the textarea. Escape in a form sends pause (forms.command).',
		'Task bx supersedes the old forms.md statement that real models have no ask tool; durable form blocks and client handling are shared unchanged, except Escape declines an ask tool question without pausing the turn.',
		'Invariant: an active terminal question displays its fields and focused choice even if its unchanged transcript item was cached before the blocked-state event. frame.layout stops prefix reuse at the active question; regression coverage checks the inactive-to-active transition and subsequent choice movement. The question event can be painted before the state event, leaving invisible choices that still accept answers if item identity alone decides cache reuse.'
	],
	needs: ['j1']
